  "title": "The knot closure is width-3 resolution, and creation is width 4",
  "subject": "What the elimination closure behind native creation is in standard proof-complexity terms",
  "conclusion": "At a gluing line, the crossing knots the elimination closure reaches are exactly the width-3 resolution consequences of the one-sided implicates on at most three variables, derived in depth one or two by resolving only on the line's variables. Every new crossing knot is implied by the same implicates and needs width exactly four, so native creation is the step from width three to width four at a three-variable cut.",
